    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, thanks. Well, what brings me in is that I feel like I’m just constantly running on a motor lately. Like, I’ll finish one thing at school—I’m a special education teacher—and I immediately jump into the next thing without even taking a breath. Like yesterday, I finished my student reports and just immediately started reorganizing the sensory room. \n\nWhich, by the way, the district just sent us these new beanbag chairs that are completely the wrong material. They’re made of this weird, scratchy nylon. I told the principal, you can't put scratchy nylon in a sensory room for these kids, but you know how administration is, they just look at the price tag. It’s exactly like when I went to buy a new lawnmower last weekend, the salesman tried to push the absolute cheapest model on me, but I know engines, you know? You get what you pay for. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, I do it at home, too. I finish the lawn, I immediately start painting the fence, I finish the fence, I'm up on the ladder cleaning the gutters. I just... I jump from one thing to the next, and I can never seem to shut myself off.",
