    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Was there a clear point when this high-energy, constantly-go-go feeling started, or has it pretty much always been your normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, no, it hasn't always been *this* intense. I've always been an active guy, but this level of just... constantly running on overdrive? That really started about eight months ago. That's when our older relative, my wife's uncle, moved in with us. \n\nWhich, let me tell you, was a massive transition. We had to completely clear out the downstairs study for him, which I had actually been using to store my fishing gear and this antique radio I was restoring. Beautiful piece, a 1930s Philco. The vacuum tubes were completely shot, and finding replacement parts for those things is practically a part-time job. I was in this intense bidding war on eBay with some guy in Ohio for an original dial bezel. I swear people on there just use bots to bid at the last second. \n\nBut anyway, Uncle Arthur moved in because he couldn't manage his stairs anymore, so we had to buy him this heavy-duty adjustable bed. The delivery guys just dumped the boxes right on the front porch and refused to bring them inside. Can you believe that? The nerve of some companies today. I ended up dragging it all in and putting the entire motorized frame together myself in like forty-five minutes. But yeah, ever since he got to our house eight months ago, it's just been non-stop.",
