    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Since this started, have you been needing less sleep than usual?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Sleep? Well, I mean, I guess I'm still getting my usual amount, maybe six or seven hours? I haven't really noticed a change there. I still hit the pillow and I'm out, mostly. But man, getting Uncle Arthur settled for the night is a whole process. \n\nHe insists on watching those old westerns on maximum volume right up until bedtime. *Gunsmoke*, *Bonanza*, you name it. And the volume on that TV... I swear the neighbors three houses down can hear every gunshot. I tried getting him those wireless headphones, you know, the ones they advertise for seniors? The pairing process on those things is ridiculous. You have to hold down two buttons while waiting for a blue light to flash, but it always flashes red instead, which means it's trying to connect to my wife's iPad in the kitchen. Bluetooth technology is supposed to make things easier, but I spend half my life just trying to get devices to talk to each other. \n\nIt's like the smartboard in my classroom. The district spent thousands on these interactive boards, and the calibration is always off by like an inch. Try teaching a kid with fine motor delays how to trace a letter when the line appears an inch below where they're touching. It defeats the entire purpose! I spent three hours on the phone with IT last week, and they just told me to restart it. Restart it! As if I hadn't thought of that. \n\nBut yeah, sleep-wise, I think I'm getting about the same as I always have.",
