    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "During this period, have you been feeling unusually euphoric or excessively cheerful?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Euphoric? No, no, I wouldn't say that. I mean, I'm not walking around on cloud nine or anything. Just... busy, you know? Just always moving. \n\nBut honestly, who has time to be euphoric these days? Have you seen the price of groceries? I went to the store yesterday just to pick up some coffee and a carton of eggs for Uncle Arthur—he will only eat the brown eggs, mind you. He claims the white ones taste like cardboard, which makes absolutely no sense because the color of the shell just depends on the breed of the chicken. I actually read this whole article about it once, about Rhode Island Reds versus Leghorns. It's fascinating how genetics dictate egg color. \n\nAnyway, I get to the checkout, and the total for just those two things was almost twelve dollars! Twelve dollars! The cashier—this kid who looked like he was barely out of middle school, wearing his apron backward for some reason—just shrugged at me. I tried to explain to him that back when I was his age working at the Piggly Wiggly, we actually had to memorize the produce codes. We didn't have these fancy scanners that do all the work for you. You had to know that bananas were 4011. If you didn't know 4011, you didn't last a week. \n\nBut yeah, no, I'm not feeling overly cheerful or anything like that. Just my normal mood, I guess.",
